cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PRISM in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "PRISM: Probing and Reporting Identity-based Shortcut Metrics"
abstract: >-
  PRISM audits trained models for demographic bias and shortcut learning. It runs a
  model over a labelled dataset through a short connector script, stores its outputs and
  hidden-layer activations, and reports performance and fairness gaps per subgroup with
  subject-level bootstrap intervals, linear probes of hidden layers against
  shuffled-label controls, and an error gallery. Runs work locally or on a SLURM cluster
  and record what produced their results.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Zakaria
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - fairness
  - bias audit
  - shortcut learning
  - interpretability
  - linear probing
  - research software
